statement.paragraph:
Consider the following problem:$$\begin{array}{l}
    \begin{array}{rrrrrrrr}
    \text{Minimize} & {   - x_{1}} & + & {2x_{2}} & & & & \\
    \text{subject to} & {- x_{1}} & + & x_{2} & \leq & 1 & & \\
     & & & x_{2} & \leq & 2 & & 
    \end{array} \\
    {\text{and~x}_{1} \geq 0,x_{2} \geq 0.}
    \end{array}$$

Consider the following problem:$$\begin{array}{l}
    \begin{array}{rrrrrrrr}
    \text{Minimize} & {  x_{1}} & + & x_{2} & & & & \\
    \text{subject to} & {- x_{1}} & + & x_{2} & \leq & 1 & & \\
     & & & x_{2} & \leq & 2 & & 
    \end{array} \\
    {\text{and~x}_{1} \geq 0,x_{2} \geq 0.}
    \end{array}$$

Consider the following problem:$$\begin{array}{l}
    \begin{matrix}
    \text{Minimize} & {3x_{1}} & + & {4x_{2}} & & & & \\
    \text{subject to} & x_{1} & - & x_{2} & \leq & 4 & & \\
     & {- 2x_{1}} & + & {5x_{2}} & \leq & {- 10} & & 
    \end{matrix} \\
    {\text{and~x}_{1} \geq 0,x_{2} \geq 0.}
    \end{array}$$

Consider the matrix game having payoff matrix $A = \left\lbrack \begin{array}{rrr}
    {- 1} & 2 & 3 \\
    4 & 3 & {- 2}
    \end{array} \right\rbrack$. Find the optimal mixed strategies and the value of the game by using the method of Example 4 in Section 9.1.
